I don't think it is implied.

> english is a tonal language.

It isn't a tone language. Whether tone plays any role at all in English (i.=
e. intonation) is debatable; it's generally held that it does, and I think =
that it probably indeed does, but the evidence is not overwhelming.

> i wonder if there are non tonal languages except lojban.

There are thousands that are as tonal as Lojban is.

